INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(14800, 0, 148, 0, 0, 0, 'Darkshore', 'Darkshore is a long strip of coast on the northwestern edge of Kalimdor, a cold and misty country of grey beaches, rocky bluffs and dark evergreen woods pressed against the mountains to the east. Ten thousand years ago it was a rich land of the kaldorei empire, and Queen Azshara''s Highborne dwelt in the twin towns of Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran, and the city of Mathystra shone in the north. The Sundering left them in ruins, and their restless dead still walk among the stones. Today the night elves hold only the port of Auberdine, and the land around it is sickening. Fel moss spreads through the woods, the Cliffspring River is turning foul, a plague has turned the thistle bears rabid, the deer are sickly, the moonkin grow hostile and the Blackwood furbolgs are openly hostile. Stormscale naga haunt the northern ruins, Greymist murlocs raid the shore, the Twilight''s Hammer camps at the Master''s Glaive and a warlock cult has gathered at the Tower of Althalaxx. In the remote far northeast, the Shatterspear trolls keep to themselves.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darkshore_(Classic) (long coast, cold and foggy, mountains east, former kaldorei wealth, Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran, Sundering, Auberdine only town, taint from Felwood); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ruins_of_Mathystra (night elf city destroyed with the Well); quest 985 reward text and Terenthis gossip npc_text 3334 (fel moss); quest 4762 reward text (Felwood source); quest 2118 description (rabid thistle bears); creature 12298 Sickly Deer spawns; quest 4811 description (hostile moonkin); quest 984/985 (corrupt Blackwood furbolgs); quest 944 description (naga and Twilight''s Hammer); quest 966 and page_text 361 (warlock cult at Althalaxx); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shatterspear_tribe (pre-Cataclysm: reclusive village at the northeast edge); DB: Shatterspear Troll 10919 spawns at map 68,21; quest 2118 description (a sickness spreads, thistle bears rabid); quest 949 (Twilight''s Hammer camp at the Glaive)'),
(14801, 1, 148, 1, 0, 0, 'Auberdine', 'Auberdine is the only night elf town on the Darkshore coast, a port of low, arched timber halls among the pines, lit by lamps and guarded by Sentinels. Elder Thundris Windweaver sees to its affairs beside a village council, while Sentinels Glynda Nal''Shea and Elissa Starbreeze see to its defense. Trade has drawn others: dwarves of the Stonehammer and Steelhand families teach mining and smithing and sell their wares, and a gnome tinkers near the inn. From the northern pier the Moonspray sails for Rut''theran Village, and from the western one Elune''s Blessing carries travelers to Azuremyst Isle, home of the draenei who have joined the Alliance. A moonwell and a lighthouse stand nearby.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Auberdine (pre-Cataclysm: only stronghold, low arched wooden buildings among pines, lamp-lit streets, lighthouse, dwarven smithy, village council, Sentinels); npc_text 5480 (Thamarian dock gossip: northern dock to Rut''theran, southern to Stormwind Harbor, western pier to Azuremyst); transports guid 2 (176310 The Bravery, Auberdine to Stormwind Harbor), 3 (176244 The Moonspray, Rut''theran), 9 (181646 Elune''s Blessing, Valaar''s Berth); quest 4761 description (Thundris elder); quest 4740 (Auberdine Village Council, Glynda); quest 965 description (Elissa''s charge); DB spawns in area 442: Kurdram and Thelgrum Stonehammer, Elisa and Gorbold Steelhand, Delfrum Flintbeard, Wizbang Cranktoggle beside Innkeeper Shaussiy, Gwennyth Bly''Leggonde; npc_text 5943 (Gwennyth, Temple of the Moon); quests 4763, 4812 (Auberdine moonwell)'),
(14802, 1, 148, 2, 0, 0, 'Mist''s Edge', 'North of Auberdine, Mist''s Edge is the longest stretch of Darkshore''s coast, a run of gloomy bays and grey beaches where crabs scuttle over the sand and Greymist murlocs keep their camps. The waters are worse. Threshers and coastal frenzies hunt offshore, and two ships, the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil, lie on the seabed north of the town, sunk with their captains when murlocs fell on them as they sailed in. Their logs still rest below in lockboxes. Farther north, a shipwrecked self-styled pirate, Captain Gelkak Gyromast, curses the threshadons that sank his ship and wants his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, put back in working order.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Mist''s_Edge (longest coastline, gloomy bays, grey beaches, murlocs, crabs; Cataclysm cultist camp ignored); quest 982 description (Silver Dawning and Mist Veil wrecked by murlocs); quest 1141 description (no boats since the murlocs); quests 2098, 2078 (Gelkak, threshadons, Threshwackonator); DB area 452: Greymist murlocs, Darkshore Threshers, Coastal Frenzy, crawlers, Gelkak 6667, Threshwackonator 6669, both lockboxes'),
(14803, 1, 148, 3, 0, 0, 'Cliffspring River', 'The Cliffspring River runs down from the eastern mountains to empty into the sea at Mist''s Edge, north of Auberdine. Its waters were once pure, but they have begun to turn foul, and Thundris Windweaver fears the wash will soon reach the town. He suspects the Blackwood furbolgs upriver, though he doubts they are the true root of it, and wants a sample drawn from the pool beneath the first waterfall, where a bridge crosses overhead. Along the banks stands the northern camp of the Blackwood furbolgs, its stores of fruit, nuts and grain heaped near a bonfire by the water, with warriors and totemics of the tribe keeping watch.', 'quest 4762 description and reward text; quest 4763 objectives (northern camp, bonfire closest to the river); DB area 456: Blackwood Warrior, Blackwood Totemic, Blackwood Nut/Fruit Stores; Grain Stores just outside in plain 148; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Cliffspring_Falls (source of the river, once pure)'),
(14804, 1, 148, 4, 0, 0, 'Cliffspring Falls', 'Cliffspring Falls spills from the mountains east and a little north of Auberdine, the source of the Cliffspring River. Behind the falling water lies a cave where rare mushrooms grow, scaber stalks and death caps that Barithras Moonshade needs for a potion. The Ancients of the Grove warned him to stay away, sensing that the cave hid a new evil in Darkshore, and their fears were well founded. Stormscale naga, wave riders and sirens, have made the cavern their lair, among them one known as Lord Sinslayer, and thugs of the Twilight''s Hammer have been seen in their company.', 'quest 947 description (cave behind Cliffspring Falls, mushrooms, Ancients'' warning); quest 948 description; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Cliffspring_Falls (source of the Cliffspring River; naga and Twilight''s Hammer in the caves); DB: Stormscale Wave Rider/Siren, Lord Sinslayer 7017 and four Twilight Thugs 2339 at x 6760-6900, y -640..-790 (cave behind the falls); Scaber Stalk spawns in 445'),
(14805, 1, 148, 5, 0, 0, 'Bashal''Aran', 'Bashal''Aran was one of the twin towns Queen Azshara gave to her Highborne, ruled with Ameth''Aran by Athrikus Narassin and home to his second, the mage Asterion. Both towns fell when the Well of Eternity was destroyed. Its broken stones east of Auberdine are now overrun by vile sprites, wild grells and Deth''ryll satyrs, minions of the demons who feed on the magic lingering in the ruins and grow stronger for it. There is one shrine they will not approach. On a small bluff on the western side, a strange blue aura hangs between the pillars, and within it lingers a Highborne specter.', 'page_text 364, 365 (The Lay of Ameth''Aran: twin towns, Athrikus governor, Asterion his second living in Bashal''Aran); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bashal''Aran (destroyed with the Well); quest 954 description (demonic minions feed on the magic, shrine with blue aura on the western bluff); quest 956 completion text (a thousand years and more); DB area 446: Vile Sprite, Wild Grell, Deth''ryll Satyr, Asterion 3650'),
(14806, 1, 148, 6, 0, 0, 'Tower of Althalaxx', 'The Tower of Althalaxx rises in the north of Darkshore, northeast of Auberdine, some way removed from the twin towns it once watched over. Athrikus Narassin, Azshara''s governor of Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran, spent most of his days here rather than among the people he ruled. Ten thousand years later the tower is occupied again. Warlocks calling themselves the Cult of the Dark Strand have gathered around and inside it, fanatics and voidcallers with a satyr, Delmanis the Hated, among them, while the most powerful keep to the upper rooms. From hiding in the nearby woods, Balthule Shadowstrike watches the cult and sends word of it to Auberdine and to his master in Ashenvale.', 'page_text 364 (Athrikus spent most of his days in his Tower of Althalaxx, removed from the towns); quest 965 description (northeast of Auberdine); quest 966 description and page_text 361 (warlocks around and inside the tower, satyr, Cult of the Dark Strand); quest 1143 description (more powerful warlocks at the top); DB area 444: Dark Strand Fanatic, Dark Strand Voidcaller, Athrikus Narassin 3660, Delmanis the Hated 3662; Balthule 3661 just outside in plain 148'),
(14807, 1, 148, 7, 0, 0, 'Ruins of Mathystra', 'At the northern end of Darkshore lie the Ruins of Mathystra, once a great bastion of the night elves. The city was shattered when the Well of Eternity was destroyed, and its survivors left for smaller villages along the coast to the south. Its glory has faded, but shards of its magic remain in the relics and small cat figurines scattered among the grass and broken stones. The Stormscale naga hold the ruins now, myrmidons, sorceresses and warriors guarding them fiercely, and a naga called Lady Vespira among them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ruins_of_Mathystra (night elf city destroyed with the Well, survivors moved to smaller coastal villages, Stormscale naga guard it); quest 951 description and reward text (relics, once great bastion, shards of magic remain); DB area 443: Stormscale Myrmidon/Sorceress/Warrior, Lady Vespira 7016, Mathystra Relic and Cat Figurine objects'),
(14808, 1, 148, 8, 0, 0, 'The Long Wash', 'The Long Wash is the shortest stretch of Darkshore''s coast, running south from Auberdine, a gloomy shore strewn with debris and the carcasses of sea creatures. Great beasts of the sea have been beaching themselves here in growing numbers, and the skeleton of a sea turtle lies in the water west of the town beside a sunken ship. Greymist murlocs and crawlers pick over the sand. In the shallows lie scattered crates of elunite ore, and a restless ghost, the Shade of Elura, haunts the water around them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Long_Wash (shortest coastline, south from Auberdine, debris and dead sea creatures, murlocs); quests 3524, 4681 descriptions (beached creatures, sea turtle west of Auberdine near a sunken vessel); DB area 453: Crate of Elunite x7, Shade of Elura 6133, Skeletal Sea Turtle 176189, Greymist Coastrunner, Pygmy Tide Crawler; Darnassus entry 165720 Elanaria''s Trial (quest 1683 wreck near the Auberdine lighthouse)'),
(14809, 1, 148, 9, 0, 0, 'Ameth''Aran', 'Ameth''Aran lies east of the road south of Auberdine, twin to Bashal''Aran and once a town where Azshara''s Highborne practiced their powerful magic freely. When the Well of Eternity was destroyed it fell to ruin, and its people did not rest. Cursed, writhing and wailing Highborne spirits still drift among the broken walls, wielding the magical implements they used in life, and one called Lady Moongazer walks among them. Two great tablets here tell of the town and its fall. In the ruins still burns an ancient blue flame, and somewhere among the restless dead wanders the spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner.', 'quest 953 description (servants of Azshara practiced their magics, restless Highborne spirits, two tablets); quest 958 description (east of the road, spirits wield magical implements); quest 957 description (ancient blue flame in Ameth''Aran, twin of Bashal''Aran); quest 963 description (Anaya); DB area 447: Cursed/Writhing/Wailing Highborne, Lady Moongazer 2184, Anaya Dawnrunner 3667, The Lay/Fall of Ameth''Aran tablets, Ancient Flame 16393'),
(14810, 1, 148, 10, 0, 0, 'Twilight Vale', 'Twilight Vale is the southern forest of Darkshore, stretching from below Ameth''Aran toward the Ashenvale border, its woods cut by the Wildbend River. Travelers do best to keep to the road. Rabid and grizzled thistle bears, moonstalkers and foreststriders roam beneath the trees, many of the deer are sick, and the Blackwood furbolgs, once friends of the night elves, prowl the vale in numbers, among them a brute called Carnivous the Breaker. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade keeps a lonely post by the road. Farther south, near the border, a Sentinel carrying word to Auberdine was ambushed and poisoned by furbolg trackers.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Twilight_Vale (southern forest from south of Ameth''Aran to the Ashenvale border, corrupted furbolgs, rabid bears, stay on the roads; BfA content ignored); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darkshore_(Classic) (Wildbend River listed under Twilight Vale; furbolgs once friendly); quest 986 description (moonstalkers near Wildbend River); quest 5713 description (Aynasha ambushed and poisoned by furbolg trackers); DB area 2077: thistle bears, moonstalkers, foreststriders, Sickly Deer, Blackwood tribe, Carnivous the Breaker 2186, Sentinel Tysha Moonblade 3639, Sentinel Aynasha 11711; area 454 has the same wildlife'),
(14811, 1, 148, 11, 0, 0, 'Grove of the Ancients', 'Nestled against the mountains due south of Auberdine, the Grove of the Ancients is a sacred place built among the ruins of an old night elf temple. Here dwells Onu, an Ancient of Lore, patient and wise. The night elves of Auberdine count the Ancients as venerable allies and heed their warnings. Onu has long awaited a message from the Arch Druid in Darnassus, and he is troubled that the Twilight''s Hammer has come to Darkshore. Two merchants keep a small camp in the grove, and Kerlonian Evershade, a Druid of the Claw still drowsy from the Emerald Dream, has stopped here for a nap.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grove_of_the_Ancients (sacred ruin of an old night elven temple, Onu, two merchants and a sleeping druid); quest 952 description (due south of Auberdine; Onu awaiting word); quest 948 description (patient and wise); quest 947 description (venerable allies, warnings); quest 953 completion text (inform the Circle of Ancients); quest 5321 description (Kerlonian); DB area 448: Onu 3616, Ullanna 4194, Tiyani 4195, Kerlonian Evershade 11218'),
(14812, 1, 148, 12, 0, 0, 'Blackwood Den', 'Blackwood Den is a cave of the Blackwood furbolgs in southern Darkshore, south of Auberdine and a short way off the road. Ursa and shamans of the tribe hold it, and they have no welcome for strangers. Volcor, master of the bear Grimclaw, has been hurt by the furbolgs and is trapped somewhere inside, unable to win his way out alone. Grimclaw has gone north to Auberdine for help, and waits by the roadside to show a rescuer the way to his master.', 'quest 993 description (cave south of Auberdine, Grimclaw waits by the road); quest 993 reward text (furbolgs wounded Volcor); quests 994, 995 descriptions; creature_text 3695 (Grimclaw rousing Terenthis); DB area 455: Blackwood Ursa 2170, Blackwood Shaman 2171, Volcor 3692'),
(14813, 1, 148, 13, 0, 0, 'The Master''s Glaive', 'In the south of Darkshore a vast blade stands driven into the earth. This is the Master''s Glaive, and Onu of the Grove of the Ancients holds that it marks a place where one of the old lords of the earth, defeated long ago, fell. Now the Twilight''s Hammer, a cult that worships such ancient masters, has come to it. Thugs and disciples of the cult camp at the site, crying glory and blood for the Old Gods, a firecaller named Radison among them, and in their camp lies a strange tome. A wanderer named Therylune strayed too close and found herself surrounded.', 'quest 944 description and reward text (old lord impaled by the glaive, slivers of power, cult worships old lords of the earth); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Master''s_Glaive (sword embedded in a fallen Old God servant; Twilight''s Hammer excavating); creature_text 2338/2339 (Glory and blood for the Old Gods); quests 949, 950, 951 (Twilight Tome, elven text); quest 945 description (Therylune surrounded); DB area 449: Twilight Thug, Twilight Disciple, Firecaller Radison 2192, Therylune 3584, Twilight Tome 12666; quest 961 reward text (Twilight''s Hammer cultists); creature_text 2338/2339 (the Hammer will still fall)'),
(14814, 1, 148, 14, 0, 0, 'Remtravel''s Excavation', 'In southwestern Darkshore, near the coast, the Explorers'' League opened a dig under Prospector Remtravel, famed at the academy in Ironforge for his discoveries. The dwarves uncovered evidence of a great society, and then horrible golems sprang from the ground and overran the site. Cracked golems and stone behemoths still lumber among the tents. His assistant Hollee fled to Auberdine for help. Remtravel, oblivious as ever, stayed behind, chiseling at the stone and hunting for his stone brush and for a mysterious fossil he had promised to send the League.', 'quest 729 description and reward text; quest 730 log description (dwarven excavation team); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Remtravel''s_Excavation (dig site, fossil, golems); DB area 450: Cracked Golem 2156, Stone Behemoth 2157, Prospector Remtravel 2917'),
(14815, 1, 148, 15, 0, 0, 'Twilight Shore', 'The Twilight Shore is the long southern coast of Darkshore, running from west of Ameth''Aran down to the Ashenvale border. Greymist murlocs have built hutted camps along the sand. One of them is the haunt of Murkdeep, for whose death the Auberdine Village Council has offered a reward, and another murloc, Flagglemurk the Cruel, prowls the beaches farther north. Near the border, naga of Blackfathom and Fallenroot satyrs lurk at the water''s edge, kin to those in the drowned ruins on the Ashenvale coast. The fisherman Heldan Galesong casts his line here all the same.', 'DB area 2078: Greymist murlocs, Murkdeep 10323 (map 35.7,76.7), Flagglemurk the Cruel 7015 (36.7,67.6), Blackfathom Oracle/Tide Priestess and Fallenroot Satyr/Rogue (around 31-32,93), Heldan Galesong 4307 (37.0,56.3); quest 4740 description (hutted murloc camp south of Auberdine, Village Council bounty); quest 1275 description (satyr and naga in Blackfathom Deeps on the Ashenvale coast)'),
(14816, 2, 148, 1, 1, 0, 'Thundris Windweaver', 'Thundris Windweaver serves as elder of Auberdine, offering sage and just stewardship of the village''s daily affairs. He sees the dangers plainly: dark forces at the borders, ancient taints resurfacing and new evils rising to topple the balance of the land. He wants the Highborne implements of Ameth''Aran destroyed so the horrors of the past are not repeated, and he worries over the Cliffspring River, turning foul upstream of the town. He suspects the Blackwood furbolgs camped along it, but doubts they are the true root of the taint, and Terenthis sends him those who have scouted the furbolgs.', 'quest 4761 description (elder, sage and just stewardship); npc_text 50024 (gossip); quest 958 description and completion text; quest 4762 reward text; quest 9633 description and reward text (Kella''s old friend, letter from Paetheus); quest 9632 description (Blood Watch proposes cooperation); quest 10752 reward text (Raene pulled him from harm''s way); creature_queststarter 3649 (Thundris gives 10752)'),
(14817, 2, 148, 2, 1, 0, 'Onu', 'Onu is an Ancient of Lore who dwells in the Grove of the Ancients, patient, wise and sparing with his words. The wind whispers to those who listen, he says, and he listens. The night elves of Auberdine count the Ancients among their venerable allies and heed their warnings, and Onu has long awaited word from Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus. He finds it strange that naga have come to Darkshore, and stranger still the Twilight''s Hammer. He speaks to those who help him through scrying bowls and weighs what they bring in long meditation.', 'npc_text 50025 (gossip); quest 952 description and reward text; quest 948 description (patient and wise); quest 944 description (naga, Twilight''s Hammer, scrying bowl); quest 961 reward text and creature_text 3616 (meditation); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Onu (pre-Cataclysm)'),
(14818, 2, 148, 3, 1, 0, 'Terenthis', 'Terenthis, a druid, has come to Auberdine to learn how far the fel moss has spread through Darkshore, for the corruption of Teldrassil and the lands around it troubles the druids of the Cenarion Circle and all night elves. Some of his brethren were rescued from a corrupt furbolg on Teldrassil, and he has vowed to stop such atrocities before more of his kind are hurt or worse. He means to begin with the Blackwood furbolgs. He takes no pleasure in killing the creatures of the forest, but with no cure yet found he believes the corruption must be held back.', 'npc_text 3334 (gossip); quest 984 description; quest 985 reward and completion text; creature_text 3693 and 3695 (Grimclaw scene); creature_text 3695 group 2 (the druid seems to understand the bear); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Terenthis (night elf druid in Auberdine before the Cataclysm)'),
(14819, 2, 148, 4, 1, 0, 'Asterion', 'Asterion was second to Athrikus Narassin when the Highborne governed the twin towns of Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran, a mage known for his physical prowess as much as his arcane art, who lived among the people of Bashal''Aran and saw to their needs. Now he is a specter caged by the pillars of a shrine in those ruins, held there by magic. Long centuries with only grells and satyrs for company have made his courtesy dry and barbed, and he fears his mind may never recover from them.', 'page_text 364, 365 (The Lay of Ameth''Aran); quest 954 reward text; quests 955, 956 descriptions and completion texts; quest 957 reward text (Athrikus his jailor, former master); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bashal''Aran (Narassin used a moonstone seal to imprison Asterion; still imprisoned after death)'),
(14820, 2, 148, 5, 0, 0, 'Athrikus Narassin', 'Athrikus Narassin was a favorite of Queen Azshara, set over the twin towns of Ameth''Aran and Bashal''Aran, though he preferred the solitude of his Tower of Althalaxx to the people he ruled. Ten thousand years after the Sundering, a warlock who bears that name holds the upper room of the tower. He stands with the Cult of the Dark Strand, ringed by the strongest of its warlocks, while the cult''s fanatics and voidcallers gather in and around the tower below.', 'page_text 364, 366, 367 (favored of Azshara, governor, tower, the spell of life eternal); quest 1140 description and reward text (soul gems with trapped Highborne souls, his power); creature_text 3663 (other soulgems, to undo his magic); quest 957 reward text (jailor of Asterion); quest 1143 description and completion text (top of the tower, ancient and powerful warlock); quest 981 description and creature_template subname (Cult of the Dark Strand); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darkshore (Athrikus trapped his people''s souls in soul gems)'),
(14821, 2, 148, 6, 1, 0, 'Cerellean Whiteclaw', 'Cerellean Whiteclaw loved Anaya Dawnrunner of Ameth''Aran in the age when the Well of Eternity still stood. After the battles at the Well he heard that her town had been destroyed and its people killed, Anaya among them, and in his grief he followed Shan''do Stormrage into the long sleep, taking his sorrow into his dreams through the passing of the ages. Thousands of years later her memory still haunts him. Wandering the woods of Darkshore in a daze, he came upon the ruins and saw her spirit there, haunted and restless. He knows she must be freed, but he cannot raise his hand against her.', 'quest 963 description, reward and completion text; creature_text 3644 (lines to Anaya); creature_text 3667 (Finally, my soul may rest... Oh, dearest Cerellean)'),
(14822, 2, 148, 7, 1, 0, 'Prospector Remtravel', 'Prospector Remtravel of the Explorers'' League is a legend at the academy in Ironforge for his great discoveries, and a trial to anyone who works beside him. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker assigned Hollee to work under him in Darkshore, and their dig soon turned up evidence of a great society. When golems burst from the earth and overran the site, Hollee ran for help, while Remtravel never seemed to notice. He mistakes strangers for Hollee, loses his stone brush and the fossil he promised the League, stops to admire his copy of Green Hills of Stranglethorn, and pauses mid fight to inspect a mossy stone. Hollee despairs of him.', 'quest 729 description and reward text; quest 731 description and reward text; creature_text 2917 (escort lines)'),
(14823, 2, 148, 8, 1, 0, 'Volcor and Grimclaw', 'Volcor travels the Darkshore woods with his bear Grimclaw, and can take a beast''s shape himself when he needs to run. The Blackwood furbolgs wounded him in the south and cornered him in a cave, too hurt to break out alone. Grimclaw went for help, bursting into Auberdine and roaring and stamping at Terenthis until he was understood. Terenthis sewed a cloak of moonstalker pelts enchanted so that the wearer could pass Darkshore''s creatures unhindered, and a rescuer wrapped in it found the bear waiting by the road. Grimclaw led the way, and at the sight of his master he rushed forward and licked his face.', 'quests 986, 993, 994, 995 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 3692 (Volcor, form shifts); creature_text 3695 and 3693 (Grimclaw and Terenthis)'),
(14824, 2, 148, 9, 1, 0, 'Wizbang Cranktoggle', 'Wizbang Cranktoggle is a gnome inventor living in Auberdine, proud of his newest creation, the buzzbox, a box with levers that lets people talk across great distances. He has set several around Darkshore, each placed near the creatures whose parts will fix its particular fault, and each, he claims, in constant need of repair. He pays anyone willing to tend them, beginning with Buzzbox 827 just south of town, which wants crawler legs.', 'quests 983, 1001, 1002, 1003 descriptions, reward and completion texts; creature_template 3666 faction 64 (Gnomeregan Exiles)'),
(14825, 2, 148, 10, 0, 0, 'Murkdeep', 'Murkdeep is a murloc of the Greymist tribe who haunts a hutted camp on the shore south of Auberdine. He keeps out of sight while the camp''s warriors and hunters stand. When they have fallen, fresh bands of murlocs come running at the intruder, coastrunners first and then warriors, and only with the last of them does Murkdeep himself come out of hiding to fight, hurling nets and battering at his foes.', 'quest 4740 description and reward text; DB: Murkdeep 10323 spawned at map 35.7,76.7 in Twilight Shore (guid 1976190, not an event spawn); src/server/scripts/Kalimdor/zone_darkshore.cpp npc_murkdeep (hidden until the camp''s Greymist Warriors and Hunters are dead and a player is near; summons waves; no quest or faction check); src/server/scripts/Kalimdor/zone_darkshore.cpp npc_murkdeep (summon waves, Net, Sunder Armor)'),
(14826, 3, 148, 1, 1, 0, 'The Twilight''s Hammer at the Master''s Glaive', 'It began with mushrooms. Barithras Moonshade of Auberdine needs rare fungi, scaber stalks and death caps, for a potion, and they grow only in the cave behind Cliffspring Falls, east and a little north along the mountains. He would go himself, but the Ancients of the Grove warned him away: their venerable allies sense that the cave is the hiding place of a new evil in Darkshore. So he asks for the mushrooms to be gathered for him, and for the cave to be scouted while they are, to learn whether the Ancients'' fears are true. He hopes, this time, that they are wrong.', 'quests 947, 948, 944, 949, 950, 951 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 3583 (Barithras); quest 961 reward text (Onu: the finding of Twilight''s Hammer cultists is troubling); quest_template_addon PrevQuestID chain 947 > 948 > 944 > 949 > 950 > 951'),
(14827, 3, 148, 2, 1, 0, 'The Absent Minded Prospector', 'Archaeologist Hollee had been proud to be assigned to the famous Prospector Remtravel, and the dig in southern Darkshore went well at first, turning up evidence of a great society. Then horrible golems sprang from the ground and overran the site. Hollee ran to Auberdine for help, while Remtravel, rather oblivious to his surroundings, never seemed to notice. Far away in Darnassus, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker has had no word from his crew in weeks. Now Hollee begs anyone who will listen to travel south and see whether the prospector is still alive.', 'quest 730 description; quests 729, 731, 741, 942 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 2917 (escort, fossil given to Hollee); Wetlands entry 1131 The Whelgar Excavation (943 onward)'),
(14828, 3, 148, 3, 1, 0, 'The Blackwood Corrupted', 'Terenthis has come to Auberdine to learn how far the fel moss has spread, and he begins his inquiry with the furbolgs. Some of his brethren were rescued from a corrupt furbolg on Teldrassil, and he has vowed to stop such atrocities before more of his kind are hurt. He has seen a few hints of corruption in Darkshore already, but no widespread signs, so he asks for one of the Blackwood camps to be found and watched for any sign of it. The Blackwood were once friends of the night elves, and if they have fallen, Auberdine stands close to danger.', 'quests 984, 985, 4761, 4762, 4763 descriptions and reward texts; event_scripts 3938 (summons Xabraxxis 10373 at the northern camp); gameobject_loot_template 14500 (Xabraxxis'' Demon Bag holds the Talisman of Corruption); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Blackwood_tribe (corrupted by satyr interlopers led by Xabraxxis)'),
(14829, 3, 148, 4, 1, 0, 'The Fall of Ameth''Aran', 'Sentinel Tysha Moonblade was sent to explore Ameth''Aran, east of the road south of Auberdine, where the servants of Azshara once freely practiced their powerful magics. Among the ruins she found two great tablets scrawled with the stories of the town and its fall, but the restless Highborne spirits fell on her as she read the runes, and she fled. She asks for the tablets to be deciphered in her place, so that a report can go to the Circle of Ancients. In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver has his own concern: the spirits still wield the magical implements they used in life, and he wants those relics taken from them and destroyed.', 'quest 953 description and reward text; page_text 358, 364, 365 (The Lay of Ameth''Aran); page_text 359, 366, 367 (The Fall of Ameth''Aran); quest 958 description and reward text'),
(14830, 3, 148, 5, 1, 0, 'The Prisoner of Bashal''Aran', 'The ruins of Bashal''Aran east of Auberdine are overrun with demonic minions, sprites, grells and satyrs that feed on the magic lingering in the stones and grow stronger for it. Yet Thundris Windweaver has noticed that there is one shrine they will not approach. On a small bluff on the western side of the ruins, a strange blue aura hangs between the pillars, and something there must explain the demons'' reluctance. Thundris wants it investigated, and the one who climbs the bluff finds a Highborne specter waiting within the light.', 'quests 954, 955, 956, 957 descriptions, reward and completion texts; creature_loot_template: Ancient Moonstone Seal 5338 from Deth''ryll Satyr 2212; Grell Earring 5336 from Wild Grell 2190 and Vile Sprite 2189'),
(14831, 3, 148, 6, 1, 0, 'The Tower of Althalaxx', 'Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is charged with keeping Auberdine from harm, and to that end she sent Balthule Shadowstrike to watch the strange happenings at the Tower of Althalaxx, northeast of the town. He should have returned long ago. Elissa fears that he has met some unforeseen danger in the forest, and she asks for someone to find him and see that he is well. The tower once belonged to Athrikus Narassin, Azshara''s governor of the twin towns, and of late it has drawn unwelcome company.', 'quests 965, 966, 967, 1167, 1143, 981 descriptions and reward texts; quest_template_addon PrevQuestID chain and creature_queststarter/questender (Delgren 3663 in Ashenvale ends 967 and 981, gives 970, 973, 1140, 1167); page_text 361, 437 (Balthule''s letter to Delgren)'),
(14832, 3, 148, 7, 1, 0, 'Tharnariun''s Hope', 'A sickness spreads across Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of all it touches, and the thistle bears have suffered worst, once noble beasts made rabid and frenzied. Tharnariun Treetender of Auberdine hopes he has a cure. He has made a trap of light to be laid in the forest: any rabid bear that crosses it should grow docile for a short time and follow whoever set it. He asks for one to be led back to him alive, and if a trap is lost he will make another, for Tharnariun''s hope, he says, is eternal.', 'quests 2118, 2138, 2139 descriptions, reward and completion texts; DB: Den Mother 6788 at map 51.5,38.3'),
(14833, 3, 148, 8, 1, 0, 'Washed Ashore', 'Great creatures of the sea have long been known to fling themselves onto the Darkshore coast and die there, but lately they have been washing ashore in ever greater numbers. The Temple of the Moon has sent Gwennyth Bly''Leggonde to Auberdine to learn why, to help the troubled people of the town. Greymist murlocs make her work hard, ringing a giant carcass on the beach just south of the town, so she asks for help gathering its bones for study in Darnassus. She cannot help thinking the strandings are an ill omen.', 'quest 3524 description, reward and completion text; quest 4681 description and reward text; npc_text 5943 (Gwennyth gossip)'),
(14834, 3, 148, 9, 1, 0, 'The Red Crystal', 'The moonkin of Darkshore were once thought gentle, almost mystical creatures, and some still revere them, but Sentinel Glynda Nal''Shea must keep Auberdine safe, and hostile moonkin now roam east of the town in growing numbers. Reports claim they are being drawn to a large red crystal along the eastern mountains, though no one knows what it is, or whether it even exists. Glynda wants it found and reported on, so that the town can learn why the moonkin gather there and whether the thing is benign or holds some more sinister purpose.', 'quests 4811, 4812, 4813 descriptions and reward texts; DB: Mysterious Red Crystal 175524, moonkin spawns around map 43-46,48-50');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(14800, 1, 4, 4, 'For a time the war with the Qiraji reaches even this cold coast. Since the gates of Ahn''Qiraj were opened, great resonating crystals of the Qiraji have broken through the earth of Darkshore, one in Twilight Vale, one by the Grove of the Ancients and one in the woods east of Auberdine. Eroded anubisath warbringers stand guard about them, and at one waits a Qiraji officer named Zod, who bids any mortal who comes near to kneel before him.', 'D:/AC/reference/mod-individual-progression data/sql/world/base/aq_war.sql (Resonating Crystal Formations 180810, Eroded Anubisath Warbringers 15810 and Qiraji Officer Zod 15813 at three Darkshore sites, one Zod at a time by pool 601053; script gobject_ipp_aqwar shows them only at state 4); src/IndividualProgression.cpp checkIPPhasing (Darkshore, Grove of the Ancients, Wildbend River, Twilight Vale phased at state 4); posarea: 4372,537 = 2077 Twilight Vale; 5064,107 = 448 Grove of the Ancients; 6434,12 = 148 east of Auberdine; broadcast_text 11432 (resonating crystals break through the crust of Kalimdor), 11471 (Kneel before Zod); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Qiraji_Officer_Zod (Darkshore, Gates of Ahn''Qiraj event, patch 1.9.0)'),
(14801, 1, 13, 255, 'From the southern pier the Bravery crosses the sea to Stormwind Harbor and back, the town''s road to the human kingdom, and Sentinels of Auberdine keep watch over her berth at the far end of the crossing.', 'transports guid 2 (The Bravery, Auberdine and Stormwind Harbor; gameobject_template 176310 Data0 967, the optional mod-individual-progression vanilla transport reroute not applied); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Bravery (patch 3.0.2: route changed from Menethil Harbor to Stormwind Harbor); DB spawns: Auberdine Sentinel at the Stormwind Harbor berth (see stormwind.json 151902)'),
(14803, 1, 0, 255, 'Drawn from the pool beneath the first waterfall, the sample proves putrid, worse than even Thundris expected. The fouled river, he warns, is only the start of an alarming trend in Darkshore, and the taint does not begin in these hills at all: its true source is Felwood, to the east.', 'quest 4762 reward and completion text'),
(14805, 1, 0, 255, 'The specter is Asterion himself, and he is no willing guest. Magic holds him at the shrine and a seal binds him, and he would be grateful beyond words for help in finding it. Decades have passed, he says, since he last had civil company, his only hosts the grells and satyrs.', 'quest 954 reward text (decades without civil company, grells and satyrs as hosts); quest 955 description (held by magic, a seal binds him)'),
(14807, 1, 0, 255, 'Onu of the Grove of the Ancients has come to want those relics studied. A page taken from the Twilight''s Hammer proved to be elven work, and he fears the cult means to turn this old magic to its own ends, so he hopes to unlock Mathystra''s secrets before his enemies do.', 'quest 951 description and reward text'),
(14809, 1, 0, 255, 'The blue flame has a purpose of its own. Asterion of Bashal''Aran knows it as a fire in which the Ancient Moonstone Seal, the work of one of the mightiest of the Highborne and the means of his long imprisonment, can at last be destroyed.', 'quest 957 description'),
(14813, 1, 0, 255, 'Onu fears what the cult has come for. The old lord impaled by the glaive is long dead, he says, but that does not mean slivers of its power do not still remain, and the Twilight''s Hammer must be seeking them.', 'quest 944 reward text'),
(14813, 2, 0, 255, 'Their tome hides worse. Its script swims and twists before the eyes until it maddens, and the one page that could be torn from it proves to come from an ancient text written by elves. The cult, Onu believes, is using old elven magic to bring its masters back.', 'quest 950 description; quest 951 description'),
(14816, 1, 0, 255, 'The putrid river sample confirms what Thundris foresaw. He knows this corruption of old, from times past, and names Felwood as its real source. A cure might yet be tried here in Darkshore, he believes, but only with help, and he hopes to call on it when the time comes.', 'quest 4762 reward text'),
(14816, 2, 0, 255, 'His friendships reach across the sea. Through his old friend Huntress Kella Nightbow, the draenei of Blood Watch send him a letter proposing an alliance. Thundris knows the isles they call Azuremyst and Bloodmyst were long ago home to his own people, recognizes some of the draenei''s foes as ancient enemies of the night elves, and promises Auberdine''s aid to its new allies.', 'quest 9633 description and reward text; quest 9632 description'),
(14817, 1, 0, 255, 'When the Arch Druid''s message finally reaches him, Onu remarks mildly that Fandral always seems in such a hurry. The forest knows that all shall come to pass in its appointed time, he says, and Shan''do Stormrage understood that.', 'quest 952 reward text'),
(14818, 1, 0, 255, 'The Blackwood camp south of town confirms his fears. With corrupted furbolgs so close to Auberdine, Terenthis warns that the town must prepare itself for the inevitable, and he sends word of what was found to the elder, Thundris Windweaver.', 'quest 984 reward text; quest 4761 description'),
(14818, 2, 0, 255, 'Soon after, the bear Grimclaw comes roaring into town, moaning and stamping his paws at Terenthis. The druid calms him and casts a spell, and with it he understands the bear: Grimclaw''s master Volcor is in trouble, and Terenthis promises to find someone to help him.', 'smart_scripts 3693 (on the 985 reward, summon Grimclaw 3695); creature_text 3693, 3695 (the scene)'),
(14819, 1, 0, 255, 'The grells'' earrings carry a trace of what binds him, a seal they have touched but do not hold. Asterion guesses that it has passed to the satyrs who lead them, and the thought of being so close to passing the bars of his prison brings him near to tears.', 'quest 955 reward text; quest 956 description'),
(14819, 2, 0, 255, 'The Ancient Moonstone Seal is taken from a Deth''ryll satyr, the work of one of the mightiest of the Highborne. For a thousand years and more it has held him, and Asterion can hardly believe he holds it now. It can be unmade in the ancient blue flame of Ameth''Aran.', 'quest 956 completion and reward text; quest 957 description; creature_loot_template 2212 (Ancient Moonstone Seal 5338)'),
(14819, 3, 0, 255, 'With the seal destroyed, Asterion is free. He remembers a world where the Well still stood and the Highborne held court with Azshara, and he names his jailor at last: his former master, Athrikus, whom he senses still lives. Already his hopelessness is giving way to thoughts of vengeance.', 'quest 957 reward text'),
(14820, 1, 0, 255, 'The tablets of Ameth''Aran tell how he met the Sundering. As the town lay in ruins, Athrikus appeared among its terrified people to guide them to safety. With a spell he could protect them, he said: while all around them perished, they would have life eternal.', 'page_text 366, 367 (The Fall of Ameth''Aran)'),
(14820, 2, 0, 255, 'Freed from the shrine of Bashal''Aran, Asterion names his jailor. It was Athrikus, his own former master, who bound him there with a moonstone seal, and Asterion senses that the old governor still lives.', 'quest 957 description and reward text'),
(14820, 3, 0, 255, 'Far to the south, the hunt of Delgren the Purifier finds the source of the cult master''s power: soul gems in which trapped Highborne souls are held. With the last of them destroyed his power is greatly diminished, and Balthule, watching the tower, sees a blinding flash from its upper room, then screams, and lightning striking the ground.', 'quest 1140 objectives and reward text (free the trapped Highborne souls; with the soulgems destroyed his power is greatly diminished; Ashenvale''s, and 1167 requires it); creature_text 3663 (other soulgems, to undo his magic); quest 1167 reward text'),
(14820, 4, 0, 255, 'In the end Athrikus Narassin falls in the upper room of the Tower of Althalaxx, his shadow bolts and terrors spent, brought down among the warlocks who guarded him, and he moves no more.', 'quest 1143 description; smart_scripts 3660 (Shadow Bolt 7641, Fear 5782)'),
(14821, 1, 0, 255, 'Anaya''s spirit is freed at last, and as it fades her final words are for him: oh, dearest Cerellean. When her pendant is brought to him, her spirit stands before him one last time. He asks whether she hates him for what he was forced to do, begs her not to leave him, and wonders how he will face the ages of the world without her by his side.', 'quest 963 reward text; creature_text 3667 (said on Anaya''s death, smart_scripts 3667); smart_scripts 3644 (on the 963 reward, summons Anaya 3843 and runs the scene); creature_text 3644'),
(14823, 1, 0, 255, 'Volcor does not stay cornered. With his rescuer at his side he leaves Blackwood Den behind, either cutting a path down to the road through the furbolgs or slipping past them unseen, and word of his escape goes back to Terenthis, who takes heart that the challenges facing Darkshore can yet be overcome.', 'quests 994, 995 descriptions and reward texts'),
(14824, 1, 0, 255, 'As each buzzbox hums back to life, his voice through it grows stranger. It slurs and breaks into hiccups, he insists that he is fine, and between instructions comes the sound of liquid poured into a cup, then loud gulping.', 'quest 1001 description and reward text'),
(14824, 2, 0, 255, 'The truth comes out at the last box. The buzzboxes were never only for talking: they also brew and distill fine liquor, a trade the night elves do not appreciate in their towns. Wizbang admits the deception cheerfully and sings the praises of crawler wine, thresher ale, moonstalker moonshine and, dearest of all, thistle bear beer.', 'quest 1003 completion and reward text'),
(14825, 1, 0, 255, 'A notice from the Auberdine Village Council puts a price on his head. Murkdeep is held responsible for the death of at least one Sentinel and suspected of sinking at least two cargo vessels in the waters off Darkshore, and the bounty is to be claimed from Sentinel Glynda Nal''Shea.', 'quest 4740 description (WANTED: Murkdeep! notice, object 175320)'),
(14825, 2, 0, 255, 'In the end Murkdeep falls on the sand among the huts he guarded, the murlocs who answered his call strewn about him, and the camp on the shore south of Auberdine is left without him.', 'DB: Murkdeep 10323, guid 1976190'),
(14825, 3, 0, 255, 'Glynda Nal''Shea pays the bounty gladly. The citizens of Auberdine, she says, will sleep a little more soundly and safely tonight, and she names the one who slew him an executioner of justice and a true hero of the Auberdine people.', 'quest 4740 reward text'),
(14826, 1, 0, 255, 'The cave held what the Ancients feared: Stormscale naga, sirens and wave riders, and among them thugs of the Twilight''s Hammer. Word of it reached the Grove, and Onu, patient and wise, asked at once to speak with the one who had seen them, which Barithras took as a sign of real urgency.', 'quest 947 reward text; quest 948 description; DB: Stormscale naga, Lord Sinslayer 7017 and Twilight Thugs 2339 in the cave behind the falls'),
(14826, 2, 0, 255, 'Onu found it strange that naga had come to Darkshore, but stranger still the Twilight''s Hammer, a cult that worships the old lords of the earth, defeated long ago. One such lord fell at the Master''s Glaive, so he sent his visitor there with a phial of scrying, to speak with him through a bowl.', 'quest 944 description'),
(14826, 3, 0, 255, 'The cultists were indeed at the Glaive. The old lord impaled there is long dead, Onu said, but slivers of its power may remain, and the Hammer must be seeking them. He bade his helper search their camp for anything that might show the cult''s intentions.', 'quest 944 reward text; quest 949 description'),
(14826, 4, 0, 255, 'In their camp lay a tome hand printed in an ancient language, its script so maddening that only one page could be torn away. That page came from an ancient text written by elves: the cult was using elven magic to bring its masters back. Onu sent for relics from the Ruins of Mathystra to learn how.', 'quest 949 reward text; quests 950, 951 descriptions; quest 950 reward text'),
(14826, 5, 0, 255, 'The relics came from a time when Mathystra shone, a once great bastion of the elves whose glory has faded, though shards of its magic remain. Onu hopes to unlock their secrets before his enemies can, and bids his helper be vigilant.', 'quest 951 reward text'),
(14827, 1, 0, 255, 'The prospector was found still at his stones, mistaking his visitor for Hollee and fretting over a lost stone brush and a mysterious fossil he had promised to send the Explorers'' League. Finding it meant guarding him through the ruined camp while golems and beasts came at him from every side.', 'quest 729 reward text; quest 731 description'),
(14827, 2, 0, 255, 'As he wandered from tent to stone, stopping to admire a book and inspect a mossy rock, Remtravel finally remembered that he had given the fossil to Hollee all along. Back in Auberdine, Hollee thanked the stars that he was safe, still unable to believe he had insisted on staying among those creatures.', 'creature_text 2917 (escort lines); quest 731 reward text'),
(14827, 3, 0, 255, 'Hollee would not leave Darkshore without him, so the fossil was carried across the water to Greywhisker in Darnassus. Leave it to Remtravel, the chief archaeologist exclaimed, to discover such a find.', 'quest 741 description and reward text'),
(14827, 4, 0, 255, 'Greywhisker had seen its like before, a fossil the archaeologist Flagongut once brought to an Explorers'' League conference in Ironforge, believing it held a power that could somehow be unlocked. The trail led across the sea to Flagongut in Menethil Harbor, who could hardly believe it had come all the way from Kalimdor. What he made of it is a tale of the Wetlands.', 'quest 942 description and reward text; Wetlands entry 1131 The Whelgar Excavation (943 onward)'),
(14828, 1, 0, 255, 'The Blackwood camp south of Auberdine showed the corruption plainly. With corrupted furbolgs so close to the town, Terenthis warned that Auberdine must prepare for the inevitable, and he asked for the camp''s pathfinders and windtalkers to be thinned. His findings went to Thundris Windweaver, who had ideas of his own about the cause.', 'quest 984 reward text; quest 985 description; quest 4761 description'),
(14828, 2, 0, 255, 'Thundris doubted the Blackwood were the true root of the evil. A sample drawn from the Cliffspring River, fouling near the tribe''s northern camp, pointed past the furbolgs altogether, east to Felwood, and the elder began to speak of a plan of attack.', 'quest 4762 description and reward text'),
(14828, 3, 0, 255, 'Then came word that satyrs held the furbolgs in thrall through talismans that channel their magic. A bowl of moonwell water mixed with the tribe''s own fruit, nuts and grain, set by the bonfire at the river camp, would cleanse those who ate just long enough to draw out the satyr corruptor.', 'quest 4763 description'),
(14828, 4, 0, 255, 'The corruptor, Xabraxxis, came raging at the camp''s cleansing and fell, and his Talisman of Corruption was carried back to Auberdine for disposal: one battle won in the war to reclaim the forest, and some hope that the Blackwood may one day be freed from their torment for good.', 'quest 4763 completion and reward text; event_scripts 3938 (summons Xabraxxis 10373); creature_text 10373; gameobject_loot_template 14500 (Talisman of Corruption)'),
(14829, 1, 0, 255, 'Deciphered, the tablets give the Circle a rare record of the War of the Ancients. The Lay of Ameth''Aran tells how the children of the stars built their homes on the shores of the Well, where Elune was said to rest, and how Azshara set Athrikus Narassin over the twin towns, with Asterion as his second. The Fall tells of ancient trees uprooted, a sky torn by magic and brother fighting brother, and of Athrikus promising Ameth''Aran''s people, with a spell, life eternal.', 'quest 953 reward text; page_text 358, 364, 365 (The Lay of Ameth''Aran); page_text 359, 366, 367 (The Fall of Ameth''Aran)'),
(14829, 2, 0, 255, 'The Highborne relics reached Thundris, and he could almost feel the taint of their foul magic upon them. If only the tools of their undoing had been destroyed in the cataclysm that ended their world, he said; he would have them destroyed now, so that their long dormant evil is never released again.', 'quest 958 completion and reward text'),
(14830, 1, 0, 255, 'The specter was Asterion, whose dry courtesy could not hide a long and painful captivity. A seal held him there, and he asked for help finding it, for the earrings worn by the grells might carry a trace of it.', 'quest 954 reward text; quest 955 description'),
(14830, 2, 0, 255, 'The earrings showed the seal had passed through the grells'' hands to the satyrs who led them, and from a Deth''ryll satyr came the Ancient Moonstone Seal itself, the work of one of the mightiest of the Highborne. It could be destroyed in the ancient blue flame that still burns in Ameth''Aran, twin of his town.', 'quest 955 reward text; quest 956 description; quest 957 description; creature_loot_template: Ancient Moonstone Seal 5338 from Deth''ryll Satyr 2212; Grell Earring 5336 from Wild Grell 2190 and Vile Sprite 2189'),
(14830, 3, 0, 255, 'When the seal was destroyed, Asterion was free for the first time since the Well of Eternity stood. He named his jailor, his former master Athrikus, sensed that he still lived, and felt his despair give way to thoughts of vengeance.', 'quest 957 reward text'),
(14831, 1, 0, 255, 'Balthule was found alive, still at his post near the tower, with troubling news he had no means to deliver. Warlocks had gathered around and inside the tower, and he had stayed for fear of missing something. His master Delgren had suspected such a gathering but not its purpose, and the scraps of parchment the warlocks carry might complete the puzzle.', 'quest 965 reward text; quest 966 description'),
(14831, 2, 0, 255, 'The parchments gave the company a name, the Cult of the Dark Strand, though Balthule knew nothing of its history or plans. His master, Delgren the Purifier, is a paladin who helps the Sentinels against demons and undead, and Delgren must know of the cult at once, so Balthule''s letter was bound south for him at Maestra''s Post in Ashenvale.', 'quest 966 reward text; quest 967 description; page_text 361, 437 (Balthule''s letter)'),
(14831, 3, 0, 255, 'The hunt for the cult''s power was carried through in Ashenvale, and when it was done, Balthule had news of his own: a blinding flash from the upper room of the tower, then screams, and lightning striking the ground. The time had come to strike, for Athrikus, master of the cult, kept to the top of the tower among warlocks far deadlier than those below.', 'quest 1167 reward text; quest 1143 description'),
(14831, 4, 0, 255, 'Athrikus Narassin fell at the top of his tower. Balthule hoped the demonic forces would be driven back, though he had no doubt they would regroup and return, and he bade that word be carried south to Delgren: Athrikus lay stilled, and the Cult of the Dark Strand was beaten and scattered.', 'quest 1143 reward text; quest 981 description'),
(14832, 1, 0, 255, 'The cure failed. With sorrow Tharnariun ordered the sick and tainted bears put down, knowing it would not stop the plague, only slow the damage the animals were doing to the forest and its people for a short time.', 'quest 2118 reward text; quest 2138 description'),
(14832, 2, 0, 255, 'Even that was not enough. The rabid bears were still spreading into the land from a cave to the northeast, near Bashal''Aran, where the infected Den Mother dwelt, and Tharnariun asked for one last killing, hoping it would be the last time he had to call on his helper.', 'quest 2138 reward text; quest 2139 description and completion text; DB: Den Mother 6788'),
(14832, 3, 0, 255, 'With the Den Mother slain, fewer rabid bears entered the land. Tharnariun gave thanks, for in these war torn lands, he said, many will not rise to the challenge of life in their new home, and choose to hide in their homes or flee to the more fortified lands of the Alliance.', 'quest 2139 completion and reward text'),
(14833, 1, 0, 255, 'The bones went north on the next hippogryph to Darnassus. The stranding was no isolated case, Gwennyth found: more creatures lay along the coastline and in the water, and she sent her helper on to the remains of a sea turtle west of Auberdine, near a sunken vessel.', 'quest 3524 reward text; quest 4681 description'),
(14833, 2, 0, 255, 'The turtle''s remains gave her a real chance at the mystery, and the idea that troubles her most is that the creatures may be fleeing the waters around Teldrassil. Her research, she says, is but in its infancy, and she asks to hear of any other beached creatures found along the coast.', 'quest 4681 reward text'),
(14834, 1, 0, 255, 'The crystal exists, and Glynda means to examine it closely. She suspects it is tied to Felwood, which lies above Darkshore to the east, and has moonwell water carried to it to be poured over its surface, since such potent magic should reveal something of what it is made of.', 'quest 4811 reward text; quest 4812 description'),
(14834, 2, 0, 255, 'Up close the crystal looks alien against the wooded hills, and a faint humming seems to come from deep within it. As the water cascades down its lattices, the opaque surface turns clear, revealing small fragments of bone and half a jawbone, seemingly a humanoid''s, locked inside a stone that even the strongest magic could hardly break.', 'quest 4812 completion and reward text (at the crystal, gameobject 175524); quest 4813 description'),
(14834, 3, 0, 255, 'The answers raised only more questions. Glynda took them to the town council, hoping it would know what course to follow, if any, and she remains content for now that the threat lies far enough to the east to be out of harm''s way.', 'quest 4813 reward text');
